Wrote the review to `/workspace/cornhole/CLAUDE_UI_REVIEW_3.md`. No game files were touched.

Summary of the main call: the panel, HUD, and pixel-art style are solid and consistent, but portrait wastes a big chunk of vertical space as dead grass between the board and the bottom controls, and the power meter feels disconnected from the control panel next to it. The prioritized list leads with tightening the camera framing and visually unifying the bottom control strip, then smaller polish items (throw-text legibility, panel row spacing, button hierarchy, tap targets) — all scoped to stay within the "simple, no new buttons" constraint.
